  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes and preferring the lottery with the higher probability. The individual explicitly recognizes and discusses the difference in probabilities (A being more likely than B), and uses this difference to justify leaning away from B, even though B offers a higher prize. Although the individual does not state a clear preference for A solely on probability grounds, the reasoning hinges on the low probability of B as a critical drawback, which aligns with the core logic of the decision reason. The justification is consistent with giving decisive weight to the higher probability of A, even if framed in terms of diminishing the value of B’s higher payoff. The information considered (probability of winning) and the justification (lower probability undermines higher reward) match the rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

